s"></a>In the News</h2><h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', s=
erif;font-size:17px;color:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;">Executive View</h3>
<ul style=3D"margin:0 0 12px;padding-left:22px;">
<li style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-hei=
ght:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 6px;">Exchange coverage loss became a measur=
able hospital earnings problem: HCA estimated that higher uninsured volume re=
duced third-quarter pre-tax income by approximately $400 million. (<a href=3D=
"https://investor.hcahealthcare.com/news/news-details/2026/HCA-Healthcare-Rep=
orts-Third-Quarter-2026-Results/default.aspx" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-dec=
oration:underline;">HCA Healthcare, <em>HCA Healthcare Reports Third Quarter =
2026 Results</em>, October 27, 2026</a>)</li>
<li style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-hei=
ght:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 6px;">Alignment showed that claims-platform =
migration can affect medical cost, as provider appeals and disputes contribut=
ed to a 240-basis-point increase in its medical benefits ratio despite strong=
 membership growth. (<a href=3D"https://ir.alignmenthealth.com/news-releases/=
news-release-details/alignment-healthcare-reports-third-quarter-2026-results-=
updates" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">Alignment Healthc=
are, <em>Third Quarter 2026 Results</em>, October 29, 2026</a>)</li>
<li style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-hei=
ght:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 6px;">Bon Secours Mercy Health-affiliated He=
althSpan is acquiring Surgery Partners for $5.7 billion, moving a health-syst=
em affiliate toward ownership of a national outpatient surgical platform. (<a=
 href=3D"https://ir.surgerypartners.com/node/12056" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;te=
xt-decoration:underline;">Surgery Partners, <em>HealthSpan Partners to Acquir=
e Surgery Partners</em>, October 26, 2026</a>)</li>
<li style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-hei=
ght:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 6px;">Federal policy improved developer econ=
omics and dialysis reimbursement: ONC reduced health-IT certification require=
ments, while CMS raised the dialysis bundle mainly to cover newly included ph=
osphate binders. (<a href=3D"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/1=
0/28/2026-21943/health-data-technology-and-interoperability-onc-deregulatory-=
actions-to-unleash-prosperity" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underli=
ne;">Federal Register, <em>HTI-5 Final Rule</em>, October 28, 2026</a>; <a hr=
ef=3D"https://www.cms.gov/newsroom/fact-sheets/calendar-year-cy-2027-end-stag=
e-renal-disease-esrd-prospective-payment-system-final-rule-cms-1846-f" style=
=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">CMS, <em>CY 2027 ESRD PPS Final=
 Rule</em>, October 28, 2026</a>)</li>
<li style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-hei=
ght:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 6px;">Overall environment: modestly deterior=
ated for payer and provider operating execution because coverage loss and cla=
ims-processing friction outweighed improved health-IT compliance costs and ta=
rgeted dialysis reimbursement.</li>
</ul>
<h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;col=
or:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;"><a id=3D"story-1" name=3D"story-1" style=3D"co=
lor:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;"></a>1. Coverage loss, not utilization=
, becomes the hospital margin constraint</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What happened</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">HCA=E2=80=99s same-facility equivalent=
 admissions increased 3.0% and emergency visits increased 5.1%, but the compa=
ny estimated that a shift toward uninsured patients, primarily people who los=
t Exchange coverage, reduced third-quarter income before taxes by approximate=
ly $400 million. Adjusted EBITDA increased only 1.2%. Community Health System=
s reported the same directional split: same-store adjusted admissions increas=
ed 3.6%, while adjusted EBITDA fell to $280 million from $376 million because=
 of unfavorable payer mix, divestitures, higher specialist fees and other ite=
ms. (<a href=3D"https://investor.hcahealthcare.com/news/news-details/2026/HCA=
-Healthcare-Reports-Third-Quarter-2026-Results/default.aspx" style=3D"color:#=
1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">HCA Healthcare, <em>HCA Healthcare Reports=
 Third Quarter 2026 Results</em>, October 27, 2026</a>; <a href=3D"https://ch=
snet.gcs-web.com/news-releases/news-release-details/community-health-systems-=
inc-announces-third-quarter-ended-3" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:u=
nderline;">Community Health Systems, <em>Third Quarter 2026 Results</em>, Oct=
ober 28, 2026</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Implication</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The results quantify the provider-side=
 transmission from coverage attrition before CMS=E2=80=99s proposed 2028 annu=
al Exchange verification process begins. Volume growth cannot protect margins=
 when commercially insured encounters convert to uninsured care.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Hospitals now have stronger incentives=
 to invest in eligibility surveillance, presumptive coverage, charity screeni=
ng and patient collections. The exposure is largest for systems with limited =
payer leverage and thin cash margins; HCA=E2=80=99s scale absorbed the shock =
better than CHS, but did not eliminate it.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Whether fourth-quarter uninsured admis=
sions continue rising during 2027 open enrollment, and whether hospitals conv=
ert eligible patients back to subsidized coverage before claims become bad de=
bt.</p>
<hr style=3D"border:0;border-top:1px solid #d5dde3;margin:18px 0;"/>
<h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;col=
or:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;"><a id=3D"story-2" name=3D"story-2" style=3D"co=
lor:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;"></a>2. Alignment turns a claims migra=
tion into a medical-cost event</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What happened</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Alignment grew health-plan membership =
31.2% to 301,200 and revenue 36.7% to $1.36 billion, but its adjusted medical=
 benefits ratio rose 240 basis points to 89.5% and adjusted EBITDA declined 3=
2.8% to $21.8 million. The company lowered full-year adjusted gross-profit an=
d EBITDA guidance, citing elevated provider appeals and disputes, catastrophi=
c cases, skilled-nursing costs, Part D seasonality and clinical investments. =
(<a href=3D"https://ir.alignmenthealth.com/news-releases/news-release-details=
/alignment-healthcare-reports-third-quarter-2026-results-updates" style=3D"co=
lor:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">Alignment Healthcare, <em>Third Quart=
er 2026 Results</em>, October 29, 2026</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Management said volatility associated =
with its Facets claims-system migration peaked in July and began stabilizing =
in August and September, but normalization exposed increased provider appeals=
 and disputes in paid-claims data. (<a href=3D"https://openfilings.org/compan=
ies/us/ALHC/transcripts/65699a58-224c-4a43-9a77-6a99a21fd591" style=3D"color:=
#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">OpenFilings, <em>Alignment Healthcare Q3 =
2026 Earnings Call Transcript</em>, October 29, 2026</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Implication</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The result weakens the assumption that=
 core-administration modernization is primarily an SG&amp;A project. Payment =
edits, appeals behavior and reserve accuracy can move the medical-cost ratio =
during migration.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Plans need parallel claims reconciliat=
ion, edit-governance controls and pre- versus post-pay monitoring during conv=
ersions. This supports demand for payment-integrity analytics and provider-di=
spute workflow, but raises implementation scrutiny for core-platform vendors.=
</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Whether Alignment=E2=80=99s fourth-qua=
rter MBR shows that claims stabilization is reducing disputes, rather than me=
rely improving processing speed.</p>
<hr style=3D"border:0;border-top:1px solid #d5dde3;margin:18px 0;"/>
<h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;col=
or:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;"><a id=3D"story-3" name=3D"story-3" style=3D"co=
lor:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;"></a>3. Bon Secours moves from ASC par=
tnerships to a national ownership platform</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What happened</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">HealthSpan Partners, a contractual aff=
iliate and supporting organization of Bon Secours Mercy Health, agreed to acq=
uire Surgery Partners for approximately $5.7 billion in enterprise value. Pub=
lic shareholders will receive $23.50 per share, while Bain Capital will roll =
its approximately 39% ownership into the acquiring entity. Surgery Partners a=
dds more than 200 locations across 30 states and approximately 5,000 affiliat=
ed physicians. The parties expect the transaction to close in the first quart=
er of 2027, subject to shareholder and regulatory approvals. (<a href=3D"http=
s://ir.surgerypartners.com/node/12056" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration=
:underline;">Surgery Partners, <em>HealthSpan Partners to Acquire Surgery Par=
