crease mostly funds phosphate binders</h3>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What happened</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">CMS finalized a 2027 ESRD base rate of=
 $297.52, up $15.81 from 2026, and projects a 2.7% increase in total dialysis=
-facility payments. However, $12.85, roughly four-fifths of the base-rate inc=
rease, explicitly funds phosphate binders newly incorporated into the bundle.=
 The underlying market-basket update is 1.9%, while budget-neutral changes to=
 the low-volume adjustment reduce the base rate by approximately 1.1%. CMS al=
so increased the home and self-dialysis training add-on from $95.60 to $138.0=
0. (<a href=3D"https://www.cms.gov/newsroom/fact-sheets/calendar-year-cy-2027=
-end-stage-renal-disease-esrd-prospective-payment-system-final-rule-cms-1846-=
f" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">CMS, <em>CY 2027 ESRD P=
PS Final Rule</em>, October 28, 2026</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Implication</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The 2.7% headline is not a clean margi=
n increase for DaVita, Fresenius or smaller operators. Facility economics wil=
l depend on phosphate-binder acquisition cost and utilization after responsib=
ility moves inside the bundle.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The approximately 44% increase in home=
-training payment provides a clearer economic incentive, although CMS offset =
part of the cost through budget neutrality and a lower onset adjustment. The =
direction favors home modalities; the magnitude depends on patient conversion=
 and training capacity.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>Watch next</strong></p>
